  "docs": [
    "Solana Address Lookup Table. Hand-authored; source of truth:",
    "https://github.com/anza-xyz/solana-sdk/tree/master/address-lookup-table-interface",
    "",
    "This program serializes with bincode, not Borsh. Two consequences:",
    "",
    "1. Instruction tags are u32 little-endian. Each instruction declares",
    "   `discriminant: {\"type\": \"u32\"}` and the compiler emits all four bytes.",
    "",
    "2. bincode prefixes sequences with a u64 length; Borsh uses u32. `new_addresses`",
    "   declares `lengthPrefix: \"u64\"`. Omitting it means Borsh's u32.",
    "",
    "The account is `ProgramState::LookupTable(LookupTableMeta)`, so its discriminator",
    "is the u32-LE tag [1,0,0,0]. Borsh and bincode agree byte-for-byte on the 56-byte",
    "meta header. The packed address array after offset 56 has no length prefix and",
    "cannot be decoded."
  ],
